## 1 · Topic and delivery

| Property | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Topic | `orders.order.confirmed` | `<bounded-context>.<aggregate>.<event>`, per the rule |
| Partition key | `orderId` | Keeps every event of the same order in order |
| Serialization | JSON | No cross-team schema contract needed yet — rule default |
| Delivery | At-least-once + idempotent consumer | Rule default; exactly-once isn't assumed |

## 2 · Producer adapter

Port declared in `10-dominio.md`: `PublishOrderConfirmedPort`.

| Port | Signature | Adapter | Payload |
|---|---|---|---|
| `PublishOrderConfirmedPort` | `void publish(OrderConfirmed event)` | `OrderConfirmedPublisher` | `OrderConfirmedPayload(orderId, customerId, occurredAt)` |

## 3 · Consumer adapter and idempotency

| Consuming UC | Listener | Group id | Dedupe key |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ReserveStockUseCase` | `OrderConfirmedListener` | `inventory-service` | `<orderId>:OrderConfirmed` |

Dedupe table: reuses `processed_events` if `persistence-architect` already created it for
another consumer in this project; otherwise this pass asks `persistence-architect` to model
it — shared across consumers, not per use case, same pattern as `idempotency_keys`.

## 4 · Retry and DLQ

| Failure | Handling |
|---|---|
| Transient (broker timeout, connection reset) | 3 retries, exponential backoff (1s/2s/4s) |
| Business rejection (typed domain exception) | No retry — straight to `orders.order.confirmed.dlq` |
| Retries exhausted | `orders.order.confirmed.dlq`, monitored |

## 5 · Configuration

Values decided for this project. The mandatory ones come from the rule and aren't
re-discussed here — `@.claude/rules/messaging.md` § Configuration.

| Property | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `spring.kafka.consumer.group-id` | `inventory-service` | One stable id per logical consumer |
| `spring.kafka.consumer.auto-offset-reset` | `earliest` | Losing an unprocessed order-confirmed event is worse than reprocessing one |
| `spring.kafka.listener.ack-mode` | `manual` | Offset commits only after `reserve()` returns |

Full shape in `templates/application-kafka.yml.example`.

